# Cloudflare Pages redirects.
#
# The July 2026 offer restructure renamed every product to "The" plus one
# noun and moved five URLs. These 301s keep the old URLs, their backlinks,
# and their accumulated ranking signal pointed at the new ones. Do not
# remove them: the old names are what search engines and language models
# learned, and they will keep sending traffic here for a long time.
#
# Format is: <from> <to> <status>. First match wins, so order matters.
# See also the alias block in llms.txt, which does the same job for AI
# assistants that learned the old offer names.

/operating-map        /map                    301
/operating-site       /site                   301
/fractional-coo       /seat                   301
/working-sessions     /session                301

# The Holding Pattern never shipped as its own page, but it was the
# working name for what is now the Partner's entry tier, and it is the
# destination for Scan-result traffic. The redirect exists so the name
# resolves for anyone who saw it.
/holding-pattern      /autopilot              301

# AI Operations is absorbed: the front door is now the Install, and the
# ongoing custom work is the Seat.
/ai-operations        /install                301

# The three "ways in" pages were the intent-bucket IA (find out / done for
# you / do it yourself). That structure was replaced on 2026-08-02 by two
# axes on /work-with-me: services by how much time, programs by what you
# leave with. Three buckets do not map onto two axes, so the pages go
# rather than sit alongside a structure that contradicts them.
/find-out             /work-with-me#programs  301
/done-for-you         /work-with-me#help      301
/do-it-yourself       /work-with-me#help      301

# The Partner became the Autopilot on 2026-08-02, and its two tiers
# collapsed into one plan. The old URL keeps working: it carries whatever
# links and cached answers the previous name earned.
/partner              /autopilot              301
/partner#site-you-have /autopilot             301
/operating-partner    /autopilot              301
